# Reuse existing helpers first

Before adding a util, helper, formatter, date/string helper, or similar shared function:

1. **Search first** — look in `@default/utils`, `@default/types`, `@default/api`, `@default/ui`, `frontend/src/shared/`, `backend/src/shared/`, and nearby feature folders.
2. **Reuse if it fits** — import the existing export; do not copy-paste a parallel helper.
3. **Extend carefully if close** — broaden or parameterize only if all current call sites stay correct. Prefer additive options over changing defaults.
4. **Create new only if reuse is unsafe** — if adapting would break callers or mix unrelated concerns, add a well-named helper (right package / `shared/`).

## Safety when changing shared code

```text
✅ Add optional param with backward-compatible default
✅ Rename via deprecate + re-export old name temporarily
❌ Change return type / semantics of a shared helper without updating every caller
❌ Duplicate formatDate / cn / envelope unwrap in a feature
❌ Dump unrelated helpers into a mega utils.ts
```

## Where shared code lives

| Kind | Prefer |
|------|--------|
| Domain-agnostic pure helpers | `@default/utils/*` |
| DTO / zod / enums | `@default/types/*` |
| UI primitives | `@default/ui` |
| App-only Next helpers (BFF, brand) | `frontend/src/shared/` |
| Backend-only Nest helpers | `backend/src/shared/` |
| Feature-only UI logic | that feature |
